// The click-through verifier on the real app (DESIGN.md 8.2 to 8.5 and the route check of 5.5; BUILD-CHECKLIST B1,
// B9). By default it builds the page (web/index.html, as `bun run build` does) and, for each scene of the
// click-through seed (test/click/seed/scenes.ts), boots bin/kitespan on a test port with the seed and the fake claude
// first on PATH (test/click/harness.ts), then stops it by its pid. With --base it checks a kitespan that runs already.
//
// The checks:
// - routes: every route example of shared/route.ts (and the seed's route variants), at 1100x800 (fine pointer),
//   834x1194 and 390x844 (touch), in dark and light: no console error, uncaught exception or failed request; no
//   sideways scroll and no element past the right edge; the route's screen and test ids show; the URL stays; no 5.4
//   line unless the case expects one; and nothing mutating before a click (D 8.4): window.__kitespanFrames, the page's
//   own record, stays empty, and the wire (what the browser saw the page send, read over CDP, so the check does not
//   depend on the page) holds only hello, ping, attach, detach and get frames and no POST, PUT or DELETE under
//   /api/. A case that expects a 5.4 line shows that one line only (principle 0). The buttons of a card's or a dialog's
//   answer row show in their DOM's order, the one Tab and a screen reader follow (FIX-Q1: on the phone they stack with
//   the main action on top, first in the DOM too). Then a screenshot, a reload, and the
//   same state again. On touch sizes, controls under 44 px are a warning. And the home-screen app's files (FIX-U6):
//   the web app manifest and each icon under /assets/ (app-manifest, app-icon-*, app-apple-touch-icon; appFileChecks).
// - history: Home, a chat, a block, a picker, close the picker; Back restores each earlier state and Forward each
//   later one (5.5 item 3). And at 1100x800 and 390x844, the list, a chat, its picker, a reload, then Escape: the close
//   goes back to the chat's entry in the same document, and Back shows the list (no dead entry).
// - actions: each action check of the seed (the table of 5.5): open the route, wait --action-wait, check that nothing
//   went out, press the route's one button (a click, or a tap on a touch size), and expect exactly the request that
//   the route names, with its fields, on the wire and in window.__kitespanFrames, and an ok ack from the server. A
//   press that uses up its state (a card, a turn, a task, the chat) runs on a fresh seed at each size.
// - flows: the phone's Terminal page (390x844, touch, dark and light): Open in terminal's link sends one type_resume
//   on /ws/shell, a reload sends none and shows the line about the typed command again, the title bar names the
//   folder by its name, and ?type=bogus, ?view=bogus and /extra each show one 5.4 line there and type nothing.
//   Iteration 1's phone + menu flow (f3e538b): with touch at 390x844 and 834x1194, + and then Add files or
//   photos closes the menu as soon as the picker opens, also when the browser drops history.back() while its file
//   picker is up (the iPhone model of checks/filepicker-repro.ts); the picked file arrives as one chip and one upload,
//   with no path in the field, nothing sent, and no history entry left behind. And two pages on one chat (D49): text
//   typed in a laptop page's message box reaches a phone page (another browser context) after its reload, the phone
//   page sends nothing, and one claude process serves both (the fake claude's own trace: no new start, one alive).
//   And a chat row's menu in the chat-list drawer (834x1194 touch, and a 900x800 laptop window): its items draw over
//   the drawer's scrim, so "..." then Rename opens /c/<chat>/rename, and a long-press (a right-click on the laptop)
//   then Archive sends one archive frame. On the phone, a swipe on a chat row then Delete and the sheet's Cancel goes
//   back to /chats, and a swipe then a tap on a group heading only closes the swipe's actions; neither sends anything.
//   And a link to a file that is not in the chat's folder shows its one 5.4 line at each size, with no failed request
//   or console error (the existence probe). And a send link's text that starts with "!", edited and then reloaded, is
//   still a message with Send (never Bash mode with Run), and nothing is sent. And a /send link, then a /bash link,
//   each opened as a new document right after the chat's page (1100x800 and 390x844): Send and Run each send one frame
//   with an ok ack, the fake claude sees each once, and the route closes to the chat in the same document, never back
//   to the earlier one. And a send with the socket down (an in-page switch, 1100x800 and 390x844): the box empties, the
//   message shows once, drawn as not sent yet, Reconnecting... shows once, and nothing goes out; a reload before the
//   socket is back puts the message back in the box and sends nothing by itself. And Settings opened as a new document
//   after a chat (1100x800 and 390x844): Done replaces it with the chat in the same document. And Settings opened from
//   a chat that sleeps, then reloaded (1100x800): Skills and plugins and Output style wait with "..." and then show the
//   live chat's facts, never "Start a chat to read it.", and nothing mutating goes out. And row 77's two session
//   settings (1100x800, with a record in the seed's registry of running sessions for a stand-in "terminal" process):
//   by default the session it holds open is in neither list and its preview says which setting hides it, with the
//   setting's link; the switch in Settings > Chats sends one POST /api/settings, and Done back in the same document
//   shows the session marked; Show sessions from other apps, off, leaves no From the terminal and the preview's line
//   with its link, and disables the second switch (its row and link stay); both settings go back to their defaults at
//   the end. And the on-screen keyboard (7.7, 7.8),
//   with a stand-in visualViewport at 390x844 and 834x1194: the Terminal pane's key bar stays above it while the pane
//   has the focus, a composer beside the pane rides on its own, and the phone's rename sheet keeps its field and Save
//   above it; nothing is sent. And a waiting card's field (the elicitation scene, 390x844 and 834x1194, the same
//   stand-in): the field and the card's Submit, Decline and Cancel end above the keyboard, and the card is back in its
//   place when it goes down. And the pane bar's Files pane (834x1194 touch): no back link beside the lit Files button,
//   Details lists no Uploads row and the session menu no Details item; nothing is sent. And New environment (D54, at
//   1100x800, 834x1194 and 390x844): the form's folder chip, then New environment..., opens a dialog (on touch a
//   full-height sheet with Cancel at the top right and 44 px rows) whose one line names the machine by the server's
//   hostname; Suggested lists no folder that a project has, and Browse shows; a filter that matches no row leaves Use
//   this folder off, as / does; on touch the sheet rides the stand-in keyboard with its field, Use this folder and
//   Cancel above it; a tap goes into a folder, the filter narrows its rows, and Use this folder sends one POST
//   /api/projects and selects the new project in the form (the tablet closes with Cancel and sends nothing); nothing
//   mutating goes out before that click. And v0.3 search (DESIGN.md 9.3, 8.3): at 1100x800, Ctrl+K from the composer
//   field opens the chat's search pane in the side panel's column with its field focused; typing narrows, Down twice
//   and one more letter put the highlight back on the first row, the query reaches the URL with replaceState, Esc goes
//   back to the chat with the focus back in the composer field, and Enter on a chat, a file, an upload and a command
//   each navigates (the command fills the
//   composer's chip); Back returns to the results with q, a reload keeps q and scope, a click on the scope segment
//   that is on shows every kind again, and a bad scope and an over-cap q show their one 5.4 line. Ctrl+K from the chat list opens /search, with the pane open it focuses the field and
//   selects its text, over a dialog it does nothing, and inside the Terminal pane it reaches the shell; Esc from a
//   chat's pane opened with nothing focused puts the focus in the composer field. At 834x1194
//   the pane bar's Search opens the lit docked pane with no first focus and 44 px rows; at 390x844 the /chats bar's
//   Search opens /search and the session menu's Search opens the chat's pane as its own screen over the chat; the
//   300-character path and the CJK and emoji names show with no sideways overflow; with the stand-in keyboard up the
//   list ends above it and its last row scrolls up above it (the tablet's pane, the phone's pane and /search), and
//   with it down the list has its height again; nothing mutating goes out. And the
//   @ picker (9.3, 6.4, 7.5): at 1100x800 a typed @ (text with no key event) opens it over the folder's files, it
//   narrows, the highlight resets per filter, Enter adds one chip and never sends (also with no row, and while an
//   input method composes), Esc keeps the text, and no @ inside a word, in Bash mode or in a link's text opens it;
//   then Send sends the mention and the fake claude gets the path's reference (messageRef) once, and the message shows the tile. At
//   834x1194 and 390x844 the @ button beside + opens it with the focus kept, the picker, the field and Send stay above
//   the stand-in keyboard, rows are 44 px, a drag scrolls and picks nothing, a tap adds the chip, and it closes when the
//   keyboard goes down. And the / menu at a mid-line / (D57): at 1100x800 "test /" (text with no key event) opens the
//   / menu's rows, they narrow, Down and Enter put "/<name> " in the field as plain text (Chat mode, no chip, the URL
//   kept) and send nothing; a filter with no row shows no menu, Esc keeps the text, no menu opens inside a word or in
//   Bash mode, Tab picks in a command's arguments with its chip kept, and Enter after a path at the end of the message
//   ("/etc/hosts", no row) sends the text as typed (the fake claude gets it once).
//   At 834x1194 and 390x844 with touch and the stand-in keyboard the menu rises right above the message box, it, the
//   field and Send stay above the keyboard, rows are 44 px, a tap (a terminal-only row on the phone) puts "/<name> " in
//   the field with the focus kept, Enter picks, and the menu goes with the keyboard.
//   And row 76 (W19d) in a chat's box: a mention chip, the seed's long plugin command as the chip and its arguments
//   typed key by key, at 1100x800, a narrow laptop box (900x800 at the largest text size), 834x1194, 390x844 and a
//   small phone's 320x568 (touch, the stand-in keyboard up): the chip cut with an ellipsis, its whole name in its title
//   and in the / menu, the field 8em beside it or flush left on its own line, Send in the box, nothing centred, the text
//   as typed (chip-layout). And D59, the new-chat form's box as a chat's composer, at the three sizes: "/" in the empty
//   field opens the / menu over the project's commands next to the box, a pick is the chip (the same layout), Backspace
//   takes it away, a mid-line "/" picks as text, "!" is text, a /new?text= link stays plain text, and a reload keeps the
//   chip (form-slash); "@" (the @ button on touch) opens the picker over the project's folder, the IME guard holds, a
//   pick is a mention chip, no match shows one line, and a reload keeps the chip (form-at); and on the laptop, Start
//   with the command chip sends the command as the first message, and Start with a mention sends it in the new_chat
//   frame, the fake claude gets its reference once and the message shows the tile (form-start).
//   And row 79, smooth text (smooth-text, 1100x800): the fake claude's paced stream (a 20,000-character markdown reply
//   in 160 pieces) on the example chat, first with the system's Reduce motion as the reference, then revealed with a
//   second page on the chat: the reveal grows on nearly every frame, is never more than about half a second behind,
//   fades its words in and ends whole with the reference's text; no fence or table separator shows as text; the chat
//   follows the end; the sent message fades and rises in here and live on the second page; the second page's reload
//   in mid-stream and this page's reload after the end show what came at once; Settings > Appearance > Reduce motion
//   On shows a short reply with no fade; and the main thread's time per frame is reported.
//   And row 80, a held chat's box (held-box; 1280x800 and 390x844 touch, a record in the seed's registry of running
//   sessions holding "Summarize the server logs" for a stand-in "terminal" process): the held line, the draft in a
//   read-only field with no placeholder, +, @ and the pickers shown and off, Continue in a copy on; typing, "/" and
//   "@", Backspace, Enter, a pasted file, a file that a picker hands over while held, on the laptop a dropped text and
//   file and Ctrl+Shift+M, I and E change and send nothing, and the keyboard's focus on the field shows; every
//   composer link (send, bash, the / menu, a command row, mention, add, model, effort, mode) keeps its URL and shows the
//   held line only; Continue in a copy sends one continue_session with the fork and opens the one copy; when the record
//   and its process go, in the same document, the box takes typing again with the draft as it was and Send is back.
//   And row 82, the panes (panes; 1280x800, 1100x800, 834x1194 touch, 1366x1024 touch and 390x844): on a laptop a
//   handle on each inner edge (a separator with its value and range) follows a drag within its range, the chat keeping
//   420 px, the arrows move it 16 px and Home and End to the ends, a pane held at its minimum by the other keeps its
//   handle and its double-click takes the room back, a reload keeps the widths, Hide sidebar and Show sidebar move the
//   focus and survive a reload, and a double-click puts each default back; on a long chat (about 10,000 elements) a
//   drag's style work per move stays under 4 ms; on the tablet the docked pane's handle by touch, a double tap, and a
//   tap on the lit Details right after a quick drag; on the large touch tablet both handles by touch and Show sidebar
//   with its name; on touch each handle shows its grip; no handle covers a control; the sidebar's filter and head fit
//   at its minimum; the phone has none; no sideways overflow, the URL unchanged and nothing sent.
//   And row 93, the panes' slide (pane-slide; 1280x800 dark and light with screenshots mid-slide and after, 1100x800,
//   834x1194 touch and 390x844): Hide sidebar, Show sidebar, Hide and Show session rail, the Terminal pane where no
//   other pane shows, and on the tablet the docked Details, each slide frame by frame (about 200 ms, the pane at its own
//   width, the chat at one width in a column whose edge rides with the pane's, the right pane never under the pane bar,
//   a closing pane's box inert with no ids, the handle hidden meanwhile), the focus where it went before; none on a
//   load, a reload, while a handle drags, with Reduce motion (Settings or the system's) or on the phone; on a long chat
//   (about 10,000 elements) each toggle's frames, late frames and the page's work per frame are reported. And row 92,
//   the link to Home (logo-link; 1100x800 and 834x1194 touch): "kitespan" at the top left is a link to / named
//   "kitespan, home" with its focus ring, a middle-click and a Ctrl-click open a new tab, a click or a tap opens Home
//   in the same document (from the tablet's drawer in the drawer's entry), and the tab says "kitespan" (row 91).
//   And row 97, Settings while no chat is live (settings-kept; the archived scene, 1280x800 and 390x844 touch, dark and
//   light): Claude Code, Models and Account show what the example project's last chat reported 3 h ago, each with one
//   line "From the last chat, 3 h ago." and no "Start a chat to read it."; nothing sent, no chat's Claude Code started.
//   And from the live example chat on the main seed (settings-kept-live, 1280x800): its own facts, no kept line.
//   And the reconnect and restart flows (R19, S14, DC9), each on a seed of its own: resume-drop (1100x800 and 390x844)
//   drops the socket mid-reply (window.__uiGoOffline) while the fake claude ends the reply and its permission card
//   waits, then brings it back (window.__uiGoOnline): one attached with replay "events" and the card, no snapshot, each
//   row once, the card open. resume-reload (390x844 and 834x1194, touch) reloads mid-turn with the card open, a queued
//   message and a draft: each row once, the card back, the stream goes on, the draft back, no overflow. resume-slow
//   (390x844 and 1100x800) reaches kitespan only through scripts/net-proxy.ts (250 ms each way, 1 Mbit/s) and cuts the
//   link for --gap seconds right after a send: the card first, a replay, each message once (a lost ack included), no
//   spinner or reconnect line left, and a message sent while the link is cut, then a reload, is back in the box.
//   restart (1100x800 and 390x844) presses Restart when they finish on /settings/about/restart during a paced turn: a
//   send held queued and never given to Claude Code, the Restarting line on the chat's page at every size, the same
//   URLs and the history after the new welcome, the held message Not sent with Send again, and one send_queued that
//   Claude Code then gets once; and in a second chat, two messages held during the wait and Not sent after it, then a
//   plain Send: Claude Code runs the held ones first, in order, then the new one, and the page draws each with its
//   reply in that order, as its reload does. offline-send-again (1100x800 and 390x844, the not-sent scene's seed)
//   presses Send again with the socket down (twice if it still shows): nothing goes out, Reconnecting... shows, and
//   after the reconnect one send_queued goes and the message runs once. resume-blackhole (390x844 and 1100x800) makes
//   the proxy's link a black hole (net-proxy.ts silence(): nothing moves, nothing closes) mid-reply for longer than the
//   heartbeat's deadline, with a message typed into it: the page notices within the deadline (the time is reported),
//   says it is reconnecting, dials again through the proxy when the link is back, gets only what it missed and the
//   message goes once; then a reload in a second silence whose old socket's frames come late, and Send on what the box
//   got back: Claude Code sees it once. resume-two-pages puts a laptop page and a phone page on one chat through the
//   proxy and has each send into a silence: each message runs once, and both pages and a reload draw the server's
//   order. resume-wake opens a chat with a long reply (a snapshot of about 210 KiB) with a focus 300 ms after attached: one
//   socket, one snapshot. resume-tail reloads mid-reply and cuts the socket right after the snapshot frame, inside its
//   tail: each reply's text once. resume-rtt opens the chat at a 1.2 s and a 2.6 s round trip: it connects.
//   restart-cancel (1100x800 and 390x844) presses Restart when they finish twice during a paced turn, then Cancel
//   restart from the dialog and from the chat's drain line: one drain line, each held send queued and then given to
//   Claude Code once, the same server. restart-now (the two sizes, a fresh seed each) presses Restart now from the drain
//   line (laptop) or the dialog (phone) with a running turn and a waiting card whose answer waits offline: an
//   interrupt, Restarting, each stop line once, the old answer stale. end-here (1100x800, 834x1194 and 390x844) presses
//   End it here and copy during a turn: both buttons whole, the plain command copied, one end_here, Wait then Ended
//   (also after a reload of the dialog), the hand-over hold with the box locked and Send again (also after a reload),
//   one send_queued. finishing (the two sizes) kills the server with SIGKILL during a turn, on a seed whose fake claude
//   finishes its turn: the new server's finishing hold (its line, the box locked, Stop); Stop ends the old Claude Code,
//   the history is read again and the stop line shows once.
//   And part 2 of iteration 4 (row 73, D60), at 1100x800, 834x1194 and 390x844 (touch), each size on a fresh seed of the
//   worktree scene (test/click/seed/repos.ts: ~/code/shop, a scratch repository with two commits, ~/code/hooks, whose
//   project settings have a WorktreeCreate hook, and ~/code/linked, whose .claude is a symbolic link). worktree-new: New
//   environment at ~/code/shop with Worktree on sends one POST /api/projects; two new chats get two worktrees and two
//   branches (the ledgers, the folders in the shop repository's .claude/worktrees with no record left in the seed's
//   data folder, git worktree list in the scratch repository, and the main checkout's git status clean after each
//   start), each fake claude runs in its own worktree with --project-config-root=<the project folder> as one argument,
//   and each Environment detail names its worktree, the "Worktree of" line and its branch. worktree-gone: after a restart and a git worktree remove, a message shows the
//   gone line with its two buttons and starts nothing, and a reload shows them again with the message in the box; Make
//   it again from its branch brings the folder back and the next message runs there; Continue in the project folder
//   moves the chat to the project's folder. worktree-archive-
//   delete: Archive of a clean worktree chat removes the folder and keeps the branch, Archive of a changed one says so
//   and keeps both, Unarchive makes the worktree again, and Delete of one with a commit of its own names the worktree
//   and the kept branch, removes the folder and keeps the branch. env-editor: /p/<project>/environment's Add variables
//   names a bad line before Save; Save, Edit and Remove each send one POST; each row shows the one mask; after a
//   reload no planted value is in storage, a URL, a socket frame or /api/ answer the page got, or the page's text; a
//   link with a saved name (?name=), opened as a new document and then by Back and Forward, marks that row, focuses its
//   Edit, opens and fills nothing and sends nothing; a new chat's fake claude gets the names and only the SHA-256 of
//   the value. worktree-off: ~/Documents (no repository), ~/code/hooks and ~/code/linked show the Worktree option off
//   with its line in New environment and in the new project's editor. Each opened state of these flows (New environment's two rows, the
//   gone line, the archive line and the kept line, the delete confirm, the Add field with a line's problem, the Edit
//   box, the Remove ask, the marked row) is checked in light and dark, and at 390x844 in each look too: no sideways
//   scroll, nothing past the right edge, and on touch the controls under 44 px (a warning). worktree-refused (each size,
//   a fresh seed whose fake claude refuses every resume with worktree_resume_refused): a message in the example chat
//   shows the line with Claude Code's own line, Continue in a copy and Continue without the worktree, and starts
//   nothing more; after a reload Continue in a copy is on, and its press sends one continue_session with the fork,
//   gets an ok ack and opens the copy.
//   And row 99, an environment's menu: env-routes (1100x800 and 390x844) opens /p/<project>/rename and /remove as new
//   documents and reloads them, and from the project page's "..." checks Back and Forward; env-rename (1280x800 in both
//   themes, 834x1194 and 390x844 touch) opens the heading's menu by the keyboard, a click and a right-click, Rename's
//   field, Esc or Cancel keeps the name, Enter or Save sends one rename; env-move (the three sizes) checks Move up and
//   Move down (one move each, the keyboard's focus kept), and on the laptop a mouse drag with its line, Esc that stops
//   one, the order after a reload and on a second page, and on touch a quick finger's drag (no long press) that moves
//   nothing; env-move-touch (row 102; 834x1194 and 390x844 touch) lifts a heading by a long press, drops it with one
//   move, and checks that a short swipe scrolls and sends nothing; env-move-longpress (row 107; 1280x800 and 1100x800,
//   both themes) lifts a heading by a mouse's long press with Chrome's own drags reported (Input.setInterceptDrags,
//   proved on a plain link), drops it with one move, checks Esc, row 99's plain drag and a click, and fails on any
//   native drag or selected text; env-remove (the running scene's seed,
//   1280x800 and 390x844, both themes) shows Remove's refusal while the example chat runs and notes-api's confirm, and
//   its Remove sends one request: both pages go to /, the one on its chat with no 5.4 line. Each puts the seed back,
//   but env-remove, which has a seed of its own. env-remove-worktree (part 2; 1280x800 and 390x844 touch, a fresh seed
//   of the worktree-env scene each: ~/code/shop an environment with Worktree on and one variable): two chats there, one
//   with changes in 2 files; Remove's confirm keeps its first line, says that the variables go and names the changed
//   worktree with its path and its 2 files, never the clean one, with no value on the page (light and dark, each look
//   on the phone); its Remove sends one request; the clean worktree goes and its branch stays, the changed one stays
//   whole with its branch, and the variables file and the ledgers go.
//   And row 111, Send now on a queued message, each on a seed of its own: send-now (1280x800 and 390x844 touch, light
//   and dark, and at 1280x800 in light each of the four looks) checks the plain queued bubble with one Send now under
//   the last, Take back from the bubble's menu, and one send_now per press, which stops a turn that only writes (the
