//   the chat is seen), and opens a link far above an unread chat's end: Jump to latest shows, and it clears the dot.
//   And R124, the side chat (the side scene's seed): side-chat (1280x800 and 390x844 touch, dark and light, and at
//   1280x800 light each other look) opens it by its visible control, asks, follows up (the history read), stops a
//   question that never answers, closes it and opens it again with the thread kept, opens a link that only fills its
//   box, and clears it, with no prompt sent and nothing of it in the transcript; the first laptop run also checks
//   Ctrl+;, the message box's /btw and the other states, and the phone's runs close the sheet by a drag (with Reduce
//   motion it does not follow the finger). side-chat-running (1280x800 and 390x844, light) asks while a main turn runs
//   a long Bash call: the answer lands during the turn, which goes on and ends with its own reply. And FIX-U2's
//   side-draft (two pages on a side scene seed of its own: 1280x800 dark and 390x844 touch light): the side box's text
//   typed on the laptop shows on the phone, live and after its reload, with nothing sent there; the phone's Send
//   empties both boxes; a question the laptop stops goes back into both.
//   And U2, turn-fold (a main scene seed of its own; 1280x800 and 390x844 touch, dark and light, 834x1194 touch light,
//   and at 1280x800 light each other look): finished turns are drawn folded to one line over their answers, each folded
//   turn's last reply in sight; the line opens and closes by press and by Enter, keeps the reader's choice over a
//   reload, opens for a link or for the browser's Find inside it; Verbose draws no line; live, the watched turn stays
//   open with the keyboard focus kept on its summary row and its rows where they were, waits while the reader is
//   scrolled up and folds at the end, a stopped turn says Interrupted once, in its quiet tag, and the reader's first row
//   stays put through a view switch.
//   And U3, turn-rail (a main scene seed of its own, whose "Try the markdown renderer" gets 24 more turns; 1280x800 and
//   1100x800, dark and light, at 1280x800 light each other look, and 834x1194 and 390x844 with touch, light): beside the
//   session rail the rail shows where 32 px are free beside the text, and with Hide session rail in every look; one
//   link per turn named by it, one current and one Tab stop, beside the text and over nothing; hover and focus show the
//   turn's card (Up, Home, End, Esc); the current mark follows the scroll; a click jumps to the turn's /m/ path and lands
//   it 24 px below the top, folded, and Back returns to the reader's place (Forward and Back again, `}` and `{`, and no
//   rail on the short example chat on the first run); no rail on touch, where a /m/ link still lands at the top; and
//   smooth text with the rail shown: the rail does not change while the reply streams, and the frame cost is reported.
//   Since the review of U3 also: the card shows once the pointer rests on the rail, and a pointer that only crosses
//   the rail to a code block's Copy opens none and copies; a click on the card only closes it; a wheel over the rail
//   and over its card scrolls the conversation; a reload after Back opens the chat at its end; a running turn's tick
//   in each look, light and dark, in --ok-fill and not the text's colour; smooth text on a chat of about 230 turns;
//   and a chat that is only partly loaded, with its three 2 x 2 px dots and the sentence for screen readers.
//   And R130, notifications (notify, on main scene seeds of its own, with a stub push service on 127.0.0.1 that the
//   server alone may send to; no real push service): Settings > Notifications' switch from a real click, the service
//   worker's registration, one push per chat until seen with its payload, headers and VAPID token checked by the stub,
//   none for a chat on screen, a card's push, the worker's notification and its click into the card's path, Show chat
//   titles, a 410 that removes the device, and off with no registration left (1280x800 light), with stills at 1280x800
//   dark (and the denied state, its line with the other device's Turn off under it) and 390x844 touch light (a link's
//   value=on and its Save) and dark (a second device's rename and Turn off). And Bring back (bring-back, on a side scene seed of its own; 1280x800 light and dark, 390x844
//   touch light and dark, 834x1194 touch light): one draft frame with the answer as a quote after the box's text, no
//   send; the side chat stays beside the chat with the box focused, and the phone's sheet closes; a command in the box
//   refuses with its line; Reduce motion; the other looks. The side-chat flow's runs press Bring back once too.
//   And U5, search-text (the search-text scene's seed; 1280x800 dark and light, at 1280x800 light each other look, and
//   390x844 touch, dark and light): a word only in a folded turn's reply shows in the search's Messages group with its
//   snippet; its pick lands on /c/<chat>/m/<message>?mark=<q> with the turn open and the word marked in that row; Back
//   returns with q and the row; an archived chat's row; no row for a word only in a tool's output; a message older
//   than the newest history page loads its pages first; each row's name as Chrome computes it, and on touch a chat's
//   lines 44 px apart; the user's own line starts with a quiet "You: ", a reply's has none (searchTextFlows has the
//   details).
//   And U4, split-panel (the main scene; 1280x800 and 1194x834 touch, dark and light, at 1280x800 light each look,
//   1440x900 dark and light, and 390x844 touch): two views in the side panel, one above the other, the Terminal below;
//   Show session rail brings the cards in above the Terminal, a file from Outputs opens in the upper half; the divider
//   by drag (the chat keeps its width, xterm's rows follow, the device keeps the share), by keys and a double-click; a
//   reload, Back and Forward keep the pair; Ctrl+K swaps the file's half for search and its Close gives the column back;
//   the window narrows to 700 px (the column narrows with the chat at 520, then one view over the chat) and widens; on
//   the tablet both pane bar buttons lit and a finger's drag; the phone shows no split. And the URL form as route cases
//   (SPLIT_CASES: a pair shows the URL's own view at every size; a refused pair its one 5.4 line). And split-review
//   (1280x800 dark and light, 1194x834 touch light): the rules U4's review found, as fixed: Ctrl+backslash on the
//   divider (focused, or after a drag) closes nothing; the cards at rest open alone; Show session rail above the side
//   chat; typing in the other half's side box makes it the URL's own view; back rows; the search pane's scope kept;
//   the folded half's head; the shortcut's note; on the tablet no pane head that holds only Close (splitReviewFlow).
//   And U1, changes-card (a main scene seed of its own; 1280x800 dark and light, at 1280x800 light each other look,
//   1194x834 and 390x844 touch, dark and light): a live turn changes three files of the example project's repository
//   while its Bash call runs (after its card's Allow) and the user two while no tool runs (one while the reply
//   streams, one while the card waits); the card under its answer says "3 files changed" with a row per file and its
//   counts, the other files left out; its head opens the turn's list in the side panel at the Terminal's width with
//   the foot line for the files left out, a file its diff with both line numbers, wrapping; the
//   Terminal goes below the diff, another row opens above it, Back, a reload, Close changes, Esc; the tablet's pane at
//   40%; the phone opens the chat at the card's one line, marked, no view (changesCardFlows has the details).
//   And P1, claude-minimum (rows 118, 119; an archived scene seed per version that the fake claude reports: 2.1.250,
//   2.1.250-acme.2 and 2.1.317; 1280x800 and 390x844 touch, dark and light): below kitespan's minimum, Settings >
//   Claude Code shows the one line in the drift line's place and Home's form under its box, in the look's --warn,
//   with `claude update` as a code span that one click selects whole for the stock build and the company's way for
//   the company's build; above it neither line, and the drift line in Settings; nothing sent.
//   And FIX-Q1, send-follow (a main scene seed with the long chat's turns; 1280x800 and 390x844 touch, light): your
//   own send goes to the end. From a search hit's /m/ link with its marks, a turn rail's jump, a changes route, a card
//   route whose card was answered (its record and 5.4's line) and a reader scrolled far up, the send's paced reply
//   streams in with the view at the end, no Jump to latest, the marks and the line gone, and a route that only names a
//   row (the /m/ link; the phone's changes route; the answered card's) gives way to the chat's own: back to the chat's
//   entry after the rail's jump, by replace for the others, so Back changes the URL and returns to where the link came
//   from (Home, the chat list); the laptop's changes route keeps its URL and the side panel's list.
//   And v0.6 touch (DESIGN-T1 3): the sizes grow to eight (626x890 and 768x1024, medium; 1024x1366 and 1366x1024 with
//   touch, the laptop's class; 844x390, a phone on its side with its safe areas), and each flow runs at the touch sizes
//   of its row of FLOW_SIZES (DESIGN-T1 3.1's table). Every route check on touch also measures control-out (a control
//   out of its box, or covered where a tap lands), blur-touch (opaque bars and sheets), name-cut, named-touch (a bar's
//   tools keep their words, or carry them as their names when tight), opener-touch (every long-press row has a visible
//   "..."), name-break (a name breaks at its own punctuation) and, on the phone, safe-area (max(base, inset), never their
//   sum); it runs again at text size 1.3 (390, 626, 1024) and in Paper, Mono and Editor (626, 1024). The new flows are
//   the long-press menus (longpress-title, -tool, -file, -upload, menus-laptop on a laptop), a cut tool result
//   (cut-output), a hold while a reply streams (stream-hold), Stop in the session menu, + and a card's foot
//   (stop-menu), Open on phone (open-on-phone), the root keyboard release (keyboard-release), the composition rule on
//   touch (ime-touch), the composer's keys beside each pane
//   (composer-fit), the medium changes layer (changes-over), the Terminal's one-row key bar (key-bar), the large
//   tablet's pane above the composer (large-composer) and its column form (column-form), a held toast (toast-hold),
//   Keyboard shortcuts on touch (shortcuts-touch), the browser pane's Select text (browser-select), D26's medium layout
//   (d26), copy and paste by touch (copy-paste-touch), a refused copy (copy-failed), PARITY's controls
//   (parity-controls) and PT-4's pickers in + (plus-pickers).
//
// It prints one line per check and a summary with the counts, writes report.json and the screenshots in --out, and
// exits 1 when a check fails (a warning alone does not fail the run; 2 when it cannot run). It starts its own headless
// Chrome on a free port from 9341 to 9349 and stops it at the end, unless --cdp names one that runs already.
import { existsSync, lstatSync, mkdirSync, mkdtempSync, readdirSync, readFileSync, realpathSync, rmdirSync, rmSync, writeFileSync } from "node:fs";
